## [​](https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/webhooks/verify-signatures#how-it-works)  How it works
```
t=1728394718,v0=9f8e7d6c5b4a...,h=content-type x-event-id x-event-type,v1=a1b2c3d4e5f6...
```

| Field | Description | Example |
|-|-|-|
| `t` | Unix timestamp (seconds) when the webhook was sent | `1728394718` |
| `v0` | HMAC-SHA256 over `{t}.{body}` — protects the body and timestamp only | `9f8e7d6c5b4a...` |
| `v1` | HMAC-SHA256 over `{t}.{h}.{headerValues}.{body}` — also binds the listed headers | `a1b2c3d4e5f6...` |

`v0` and `v1` are both included on every request. `v0` includes the timestamp and body; `v1` additionally binds the listed headers.

2. **Build signed payload**: Concatenate `timestamp.headerNames.headerValues.rawBody`
4. **Compare signatures**: Use timing-safe comparison to match expected vs. provided
5. **Verify timestamp**: Ensure the webhook isn’t too old (prevents replay attacks)

